 ## Commands
 
 - `list` prints one line per book, in the order of the file. `--status to-read|reading|done` keeps
-  only the books in that state.
+  only the books in that state. `--tag <tag>` keeps the books that carry the tag, whatever its case;
+  given several times, a book has to carry all of them.
 - `add` puts a book at the end of the list. `--title`, `--author` and `--pages` are required;
   `--status` (default `to-read`), `--rating` (1 to 5) and `--tags` (separated by commas) are optional.
-- `stats` counts the books, in all and per state.
+  A book whose title and author are already in the list (case and surrounding spaces aside) is refused.
+- `finish <start of a title>` marks the one book whose title starts that way as `done`; `--rating`
+  (1 to 5) records a rating with it. No match, or more than one, is an error.
+- `stats` counts the books, in all and per state, adds up the pages of the finished ones and gives
+  the average rating to one decimal (`-` when no book has a rating).
 
 A command that cannot do what was asked prints `error: ...` on stderr and exits with 1; the file is
 left as it was.
